# primates5: five catarrhines, a node apart from human to macaque (substitutions per site, from the VGP 577-way's tree
# cut down to these five with their pairwise distances kept; URLs are the 577-way's).  With the suite's --branchScale
# 2.0 the ancestors' ingroups are 0.013 (human-chimp), 0.021, 0.043 and 0.085 (the root) apart, the range where most of a
# big mammal alignment's ancestors lie (in the 447-way, 72% of them are under 0.05) and busco5 has none.
#   GCA_000001405.15  human (GRCh38 no-alt analysis set, as in busco5: the CTCF cCREs are on it)
#   GCF_028858775.2   chimpanzee (T2T mPanTro3)   -> the human-chimp node
#   GCF_029281585.2   gorilla (T2T mGorGor1)      -> the Homininae node
#   GCF_028885655.2   Sumatran orangutan (T2T mPonAbe1) -> the Hominidae node
#   GCF_037993035.1   crab-eating macaque (T2T-MFA8) -> the catarrhine root
((((GCF_028858775.2:0.00304,GCA_000001405.15:0.00362):0.00158,GCF_029281585.2:0.00516):0.00530,GCF_028885655.2:0.01116):0.00905,GCF_037993035.1:0.02230);

